> A calculation before fitting

A greedy first choice with probability.6 followed by.51 gives joint probability.306. Keeping the alternative.4 branch allows a.99 continuation and joint probability.396. Beam width can change the best sequence without changing its model probability.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/beam_search_worked.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -lpthread -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main(){namespace n=dm::nn;double computed=n::exp(n::log(n::scalar(.4,n::DType::Float64))+n::log(n::scalar(.99,n::DType::Float64))).item(),analytic=.396;if(std::abs(computed-analytic)>2e-6)throw std::runtime_error("hand calculation differs from native primitives");std::print("| native calculation | analytic reference |\n|---:|---:|\n| {:.9f} | {:.9f} |\n",computed,analytic);dm::graphics::RPlot::create().bars(std::vector<double>{0,1},std::vector<double>{computed,analytic},"worked reference",{37,99,235}).ylim(0,std::max(.5,std::max(computed,analytic)*1.2)).x_label("0 = native calculation;1 = analytic reference").y_label("Toy objective or diagnostic value").title("beam search hand calculation").size(1000,550).save_svg("build/beam_search_worked.svg");}
```
